           ~38px out of step — "Season starts" sits at a different
           height in each card. Same for the format line. Give the row
           enough width to stay on one line and every card aligns for
           free, at any content length.
       (2) SCALE. A 720px column of cards on a 2000px monitor was most
           of why this page still read small even after the type bump.

       Prose stays at 720px — 75ch is the right measure for reading.
       A spec grid is not prose, so it gets its own width.

